 "notes": "C4 and P21 both target the authors' interpretation of the weak centering-violating reflections in Fig. 2(c) relative to Li et al.'s intermediate Bmab phase: C4 argues their pressure dependence favors Bmab over twinning, while P21 notes twinned Bmab produces the same reflections so they cannot exclude Bmab (judged 'partly'). C5 asks for high-pressure powder XRD because single-crystal lattice parameters cannot resolve the tiny distortion to exclude Bmab; P9 raises the same resolution limitation near the transition but asks for statistical tests and angular resolution bounds rather than new PXRD measurements (judged 'partly'). C14 is partly matched by P18 (tension between the first-order jump in beta and mean-field DFT fits) and P10 (critique of the 3-point mean-field fits). C18 relies on SI refinement tables (N/p and GoF at high pressure) not present in the main text.",
